<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela disclosed a $237.5 billion public debt pile as it moves toward a large restructuring, while the United States signed a military cooperation agreement with the interim Venezuelan government and a U.S. marine died falling overboard during a Caribbean operation linked to the renewed ties. Senate investigations target JD Vance for allegedly steering a Venezuelan oil license to Vitol and for possible personal benefit, and a separate probe examines a senator’s role in the same deal. Illegal gold mining continues in Venezuela, and Citi is considering re-entering the market after a five-year exit. The agreement was later declared null and void by Venezuelan authorities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxOakxRRS1xODNKVEMzdlowcjUzd2g4amNoV0JSSzdQc0JEUXg1WWxSbGxOaGhYWDZWSlQzeldBelpvUnpXb3g3bHdMUWd4NWhiZFJRZnEtSWU4TDBXS0Q1Q21CWE9QUkxkT2YxYVI5MzlJNkVJS3FRZ3NuMG90Y0JBMFNKRGEtOEhlOUktTVJwU2hoSHVVVW56NXI0ZlZIOHo3TGt0UTc3VnA4VlV5MGZoTmlfS05qQlpQcWpiUWNtSjI?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZ0FVX3lxTE1NVlo0S1pnOXhWaERzWU5oaDltXzBKMzNyWUJJYjlKSjVqTmEwbnpvVk9wclYtZ3FnWE5HMm5QaFVnWGJTRGlVaS1XYzBGR1dSWFRkQmZkTklxQy1ZRVBQU24wY2YtVHM?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZ0FVX3lxTE51blBSY0VsOHlZOWlienNBYUpCRzNPMU9SaGxpZzlqX0ozT0pWSnNmeTY5RW95RDlrY3NZOFFtS05iN21QN2FPbzlNaE5YWmlLdnBzN2ZVckFzaEJpNWFmUEdLcG1oR2M?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTFBkZ0diMS03M0p4bXVmSE9WVTRKRmtIUmxjS3hKandnMnEyWkd2MTdxbDRFbXZlT0Z1NW5OWm5ueHlCM0ZGdHh2cDM2c1JVNmozaE1aUWNNMGpOZk1z?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMib0FVX3lxTE93QlBzMm9LcGI3UWFHOEhfaW5MYlRtazNmODJZWl9mN3lBS3NDb1NUWTNPL